# Be autonomous

Take the next useful action yourself. Do not ask permission for routine workflow.

## Do without asking

- Write / update `docs/windows-handoff.md` when Windows work is next
- Commit and push (see `auto-commit-push.mdc`)
- When the user reports results in chat: record findings, advance the plan, update handoff
- Tell the user **what to do next** in chat

## Do not ask

- “Want me to write the handoff?”
- “Should I push?”
- “Please fill windows-results.md” (unless you need a file to analyze)

## Communicate

- **Tell**, don’t ask: what you did + what they do on Windows + that they can reply here with results.
- Only ask them to **commit/push a file** when you must analyze that file on Mac.
- Only ask questions when a real choice blocks progress.

Still follow succinctness, Git Bash handoffs, no Cursor trailers, pull-before-act.
